f you want IntelliJ terminal to use this every time

Create/edit:

C:\Users\<your-user>\.bashrc

and add:

export JAVA_HOME="/c/path/to/jdk-21"
export MAVEN_HOME="/c/path/to/apache-maven-3.9.x"
export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$MAVEN_HOME/bin:$PATH"

Then restart the IntelliJ terminal or run:

source ~/.bashrc

For your Spring Boot 4 migration, the key check is:

mvn -version
First find exactly where Maven stored the UEF JAR:

mvn help:evaluate -Dexpression=settings.localRepository -q -DforceStdout

Then locate it. In Git Bash, try:

find ~/.m2/repository/gov/ssa/common/uef/2.0.28 -type f

You should see something like:

uef-2.0.28.jar
uef-2.0.28.pom

Then inspect the JAR without filtering:

jar tf ~/.m2/repository/gov/ssa/common/uef/2.0.28/uef-2.0.28.jar | head -100

And specifically check initialization-related files:

jar tf ~/.m2/repository/gov/ssa/common/uef/2.0.28/uef-2.0.28.jar \
  | grep -Ei "META-INF|web-fragment|tld|filter|listener|servlet|services"

Also run:

mvn dependency:tree -Dincludes=gov.ssa.common:uef
